they've arrested him at boulogne how do you know show gland told me when yesterday

01:03:02.240 --> 01:03:13.110
why didn't you tell me when i asked you i don't know why are you telling me now because i thought

01:03:13.110 --> 01:03:18.900
you might do something for our moon you have influence at court didn't you ask your friend

01:03:18.900 --> 01:03:29.460
chauvelin for help promise me that don't trust him he promised you the life of your brother

01:03:31.440 --> 01:03:32.560
What did you give him in exchange?

01:03:33.020 --> 01:03:43.500
What happened to you, Percy? You hate me.

01:03:46.290 --> 01:03:47.990
Why did you denounce the Marquis de Saint-Cyr?

01:03:49.140 --> 01:03:49.840
So that's it.

01:03:50.940 --> 01:03:53.200
Why did you never ask me what the Marquis de Saint-Cyr did to me?

01:03:53.380 --> 01:03:54.260
You didn't even know him.

01:03:56.620 --> 01:03:58.760
No, I didn't even know him.

01:04:00.920 --> 01:04:05.950
But I knew his son. I was only 17 when he asked me to marry him.

01:04:07.030 --> 01:04:08.570
His father heard about it and had me arrested.

01:04:09.830 --> 01:04:14.340
He went to San Lazar. Do you know what San Lazar is?

01:04:16.740 --> 01:04:18.340
Do you know the sort of women that are sent there?

01:04:20.730 --> 01:04:23.770
I killed myself. Only. Only what?

01:04:24.520 --> 01:04:27.960
The revolution came. The ever-glorious 14th of July.

01:04:29.330 --> 01:04:29.970
And I was free.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:34.740
Why this tardy explanation?

01:04:36.270 --> 01:04:38.890
I asked you once if you sent the Saint-Cyrs to the guillotine. You said yes.

01:04:40.100 --> 01:04:41.540
You believed so easily, didn't you?

01:04:43.850 --> 01:04:49.340
Yet I still ask myself, am I really guilty of their death?

01:04:50.370 --> 01:04:51.470
If not you, who is?

01:04:52.540 --> 01:04:54.720
He plotted with Austria. I told a friend.

01:04:55.700 --> 01:04:58.630
A man whom I thought a friend. He denounced him.

01:05:01.060 --> 01:05:08.470
Who was that friend? Was it Chauvelin?

01:05:13.960 --> 01:05:15.360
He promised you your brother's life.

01:05:17.260 --> 01:05:18.360
What price did you pay for it?

01:05:20.690 --> 01:05:21.870
What price did you pay for it?

01:05:24.370 --> 01:05:25.330
I paid a horrible price.

01:05:30.460 --> 01:05:30.860
How?

01:05:35.680 --> 01:05:37.320
Books had a scrap of paper in his cuff.

01:05:38.120 --> 01:05:40.840
I read it and told Chauvelin that the Pimpernel would be in the library at midnight.

01:05:41.960 --> 01:05:43.600
And was he in the library at midnight?

01:05:44.460 --> 01:05:47.290
Chauvelin says he wasn't, but I think he's lying.

01:05:49.620 --> 01:05:52.540
Through my betrayal, a noble and generous man might lose his life.

01:05:53.590 --> 01:05:55.990
What am I to do, Percy? How can I warn him?

01:05:56.690 --> 01:05:58.750
Warn him? Against what?

