that threatens him if he goes back to France my dear if he's the kind of

01:06:04.220 --> 01:06:07.730
lunatic I take him to be your warning won't stop him but he might be going to

01:06:07.730 --> 01:06:13.030
his death well that's all the fellow lives for besides he doesn't know you're

01:06:13.030 --> 01:06:18.320
in love with him not in love with him I admire his heroism but I don't love him

01:06:18.320 --> 01:06:23.510
well but you do only you don't know it I didn't know it myself until a moment ago

01:06:23.730 --> 01:06:29.220
Percy please don't joke about it it's no joke believe me

01:06:31.600 --> 01:06:37.150
dangerous game falling in love with a phantom my dear for all you know he may be a married man

01:06:38.320 --> 01:06:46.890
deeply in love with his wife never why not would any man who was in love with his wife

01:06:46.890 --> 01:06:59.070
leave her continually to face death would you me i'm much more romantic than you think

01:07:00.320 --> 01:07:03.860
In a case like that, I wouldn't leave you, not even to go to my tailor.

01:07:04.080 --> 01:07:06.830
The horses are ready, sir.

01:07:07.550 --> 01:07:08.170
Thank you, Brinker.

01:07:08.650 --> 01:07:09.410
Are you going away?

01:07:09.980 --> 01:07:11.000
Oh, yes, didn't I tell you?

01:07:11.740 --> 01:07:13.040
Important business in town.

01:07:14.350 --> 01:07:15.050
Goodbye, my dear.

01:07:16.520 --> 01:07:17.660
Your tailors, I suppose.

01:07:18.050 --> 01:07:20.110
Not only my tailors, but also my bootmakers.

01:07:21.060 --> 01:07:24.830
And incidentally, I want to see what my influence is worth at court.

01:07:25.280 --> 01:07:26.560
That little matter of your brother's.

01:07:28.470 --> 01:07:29.190
Perhaps I can help.

01:07:31.530 --> 01:07:34.180
Percy, if you could, I'd love you all my life.

01:07:36.070 --> 01:07:39.880
Gad, I must remember that, my dear.

01:07:42.210 --> 01:07:42.430
Goodbye.

01:08:11.520 --> 01:08:13.260
It's six o'clock, my lady.

01:08:14.970 --> 01:08:16.250
Suppose you want me to leave this room?

01:08:18.080 --> 01:08:20.000
I've never been here quite alone, have I?

01:08:20.430 --> 01:08:21.170
No, my lady.

01:08:22.310 --> 01:08:23.490
All right, Benker. Thank you.

01:09:08.640 --> 01:09:29.800
a letter to be delivered into your ladyship's hand. from sir Percy? no madame.

01:09:30.120 --> 01:09:31.720
From His Excellency, the French Ambassador.

01:10:00.760 --> 01:10:01.740
Where is Monsieur Chauvelin?

01:10:01.900 --> 01:10:03.760
He left this morning for France, madame.

01:10:05.450 --> 01:10:20.370
All right, thank you. Brinker, carriage.

01:11:02.400 --> 01:11:12.740
Lady Blakeney, what's happened?

01:11:13.360 --> 01:11:15.500
There's no time to waste in talking. Just listen to me.

01:11:16.170 --> 01:11:18.830
Your leader and friend, the Scarlet Pimpernel, my husband...

01:11:18.830 --> 01:11:21.730
How do you know that? Don't ask me questions now. He's in peril.

01:11:22.760 --> 01:11:25.800
Chauvelin knows that Percy Blakeney and the Scarlet Pimpernel are the same.

01:11:26.020 --> 01:11:27.180
How did Chauvelin come to know?

01:11:31.060 --> 01:11:34.760
Do you mean to say that you betrayed him?

01:11:34.980 --> 01:11:36.700
Yes, yes, yes, I betrayed him. Never mind how.

01:11:36.860 --> 01:11:37.360
Just tell me this.

01:11:37.820 --> 01:11:39.200
Has Percy left for Boulogne?

01:11:39.580 --> 01:11:39.900
Yes.

01:11:40.850 --> 01:11:41.470
To save my brother?

01:11:41.630 --> 01:11:42.270
And de Tourne?

01:11:42.880 --> 01:11:44.280
What is their meeting place at Boulogne?

01:11:46.030 --> 01:11:46.350
Why?

01:11:47.460 --> 01:11:48.320
Do you want to...

01:11:48.500 --> 01:11:49.620
Oh, look at me, man.

01:11:49.960 --> 01:11:52.200
Do I look like a woman who wants to send her husband to his death?

01:11:52.610 --> 01:11:55.630
I want to find Percy, to warn him, to save him, or to die with...

01:12:00.000 --> 01:12:00.400
I'll go with you.

01:12:04.950 --> 01:12:05.770
Can you bring your friends?

01:12:07.210 --> 01:12:07.750
Ten of them.

01:12:08.940 --> 01:12:09.780
The rest are in France.

01:12:11.220 --> 01:12:12.560
Percy has forbidden us to go over.

01:12:13.780 --> 01:12:15.360
It'll be the first time we've ever disobeyed him.

01:12:20.050 --> 01:12:22.150
Save Percy even if I had to kill Chauvelin.

01:12:23.560 --> 01:12:26.470
And if he goes to the guillotine, go after him.

01:12:32.750 --> 01:12:33.940
There you are, citizens!

01:12:34.740 --> 01:12:36.880
Boulogne has a guillotine of its own now!

01:12:37.830 --> 01:12:38.530
It was Paris!

01:12:38.810 --> 01:12:39.470
That's nothing!

01:12:40.270 --> 01:12:41.990
Half the towns in France have got them!

01:12:49.930 --> 01:12:53.120
So much for the bait.

01:12:54.460 --> 01:12:55.080
Now for the trap.

01:12:55.980 --> 01:12:57.600
We can't afford to make any mistakes this time.

01:12:57.870 --> 01:12:59.790
Remember, it's either the Plimpernel or ourselves.

