with a pack a peasant with a beard anything listen my friend the next time you want to put on a false

01:13:28.060 --> 01:13:29.280
Choose a good one.

01:13:30.160 --> 01:13:32.100
that wouldn't deceive a child.

01:13:34.880 --> 01:13:36.820
Clumsy idiot! Let go, you!

01:13:37.650 --> 01:13:40.270
I'll teach him to pull the best beard in Boulogne.

01:13:49.490 --> 01:13:53.740
You'll hear more of this woman I am, one of the few in our street.

01:13:55.280 --> 01:13:58.300
He'd buy soldiers and them search to see if I was a man.

01:14:14.700 --> 01:14:19.120
I was 20 years younger. That's what I should be.

01:14:19.580 --> 01:14:21.060
Bravo, uncle. That's the spirit.

01:14:22.530 --> 01:14:23.990
Where are you boys serving now?

01:14:24.530 --> 01:14:25.690
Oh, we're on leave.

01:14:26.470 --> 01:14:29.270
Teeding away the hearts of the girls of Buroying.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:30.980
Well, sir, I'm in love.

01:14:32.980 --> 01:14:34.700
It's the wife of another man.

01:14:35.170 --> 01:14:36.670
No, it's my own.

01:14:38.630 --> 01:14:41.830
Captain, I'll tell you a secret.

01:14:44.340 --> 01:14:48.880
You and I are the only men in France who are in love with our wives.

01:14:49.000 --> 01:14:50.520
All right, let's drink to it.

01:14:51.540 --> 01:14:52.620
Well, here's to it.

01:14:55.300 --> 01:14:59.970
But it'll be hard for you.

01:15:00.120 --> 01:15:02.080
Are you willing to leave her for this war with England?

01:15:02.320 --> 01:15:03.240
Do you think that's coming?

01:15:03.580 --> 01:15:08.100
Surely! We shall have to teach perfidious Albion a lesson!

01:15:08.660 --> 01:15:11.280
Well, it won't take us long to get across the channel, will it, boys?

01:15:12.880 --> 01:15:16.340
Well, gentlemen, good luck and...

01:15:18.420 --> 01:15:26.710
The Tournai was brought here from Paris yesterday, the same prisoner's armhole.

01:15:26.910 --> 01:15:29.390
I thought so. Chauvelin's using them as a plea.

01:15:33.320 --> 01:15:37.800
Search every incoming ship, even the smallest fishing boat.

01:15:38.200 --> 01:15:41.120
And you, Detourney and Sanchez, have escaped.

01:15:41.260 --> 01:15:42.400
To escape? How?

01:15:43.290 --> 01:15:45.250
God knows. The Pimpernel knows.

01:15:45.960 --> 01:15:47.080
Someone will pay for this.

01:15:47.840 --> 01:15:49.400
Where are the jailers? Missy.

01:15:51.300 --> 01:15:51.660
Shoveler.

01:15:51.870 --> 01:15:53.350
How dare you burst in like this? Who are you?

01:15:53.410 --> 01:15:54.210
The jailer from the prison.

01:15:54.390 --> 01:15:55.130
So you're one of the...

01:15:55.130 --> 01:15:56.250
No fault of mine, citizen.

01:15:56.620 --> 01:15:58.040
The head jailer and the others would have killed me

01:15:58.040 --> 01:15:59.960
if I hadn't taken the money to free those accursed...

01:16:00.030 --> 01:16:00.630
What?

01:16:01.280 --> 01:16:02.440
Pimpernel is taking them to England.

01:16:03.010 --> 01:16:04.170
Promises all jobs there.

01:16:04.880 --> 01:16:08.700
I'm a good patriot citizen, Chevalon, and I'm not losing my head,

01:16:09.580 --> 01:16:11.940
because I've got some information that will save yours.

01:16:13.470 --> 01:16:14.230
What is it worth?

01:16:15.160 --> 01:16:15.680
What do you know?

01:16:16.690 --> 01:16:19.190
Where you can find the scarlet Pimpernel.

01:16:20.250 --> 01:16:20.690
Out with it?

01:16:21.500 --> 01:16:21.760
Where?

01:16:24.290 --> 01:16:27.290
To meet him at 10 o'clock at the Lyon d'Or.

01:16:29.280 --> 01:16:29.700
Take him away.

01:16:35.020 --> 01:16:36.660
Ten o'clock at the Lyon d'Or.

01:17:00.120 --> 01:17:06.280
We must wait for the signal. Brogard waves a lantern across the window for safe, up and down for danger.

01:17:07.710 --> 01:17:14.450
Look, there's a signal. Safe.

01:17:17.150 --> 01:17:20.900
You've got all the roads watched? Every corner and the beach.

01:17:21.480 --> 01:17:24.420
And a troop of dragoons to surround the place? Waiting outside.

01:17:25.250 --> 01:17:26.970
Come on, then. The Léon d'Or.

01:17:44.040 --> 01:17:47.760
What do you want here? This is no place for one of your sort.

01:17:49.370 --> 01:17:51.470
I'm the sort that pays well, Citizen Brogau.

01:17:52.900 --> 01:17:53.520
For what?

01:17:55.250 --> 01:17:56.370
For a seat by the fire.

01:18:00.670 --> 01:18:20.940
I'll wait here for a friend of mine and yours.

01:18:21.370 --> 01:18:23.050
What should I know of your friends?

01:18:23.670 --> 01:18:26.810
You signaled to him just now. You must be expecting him. What time?

01:18:30.090 --> 01:18:30.590
What time?

01:18:33.050 --> 01:18:33.830
10 o'clock.

01:19:16.600 --> 01:19:19.470
It is in progress under arrest.

01:19:27.800 --> 01:19:28.320
What for?

01:19:28.870 --> 01:19:29.690
Betraying the Republic.

01:19:30.410 --> 01:19:34.160
Helping the enemies of France, harbouring a gang of dangerous criminals,

01:19:34.820 --> 01:19:36.440
smuggling aristocrats out of the country.

01:19:36.640 --> 01:19:37.360
That's a lie.

01:19:37.720 --> 01:19:38.820
You've got one chance.

01:19:39.230 --> 01:19:41.790
Take it or I'll hang you now from your own sign.

01:19:42.950 --> 01:19:46.010
The leader of your gang is coming here tonight, isn't he?

01:19:47.300 --> 01:19:47.740
Isn't he?

01:19:49.560 --> 01:19:49.940
Yes.

01:19:50.190 --> 01:19:50.350
What?

01:19:52.870 --> 01:19:55.580
He ordered his boat to be off the point at 10 o'clock.

01:19:55.740 --> 01:19:58.160
Ah, but he'll call here first for his passengers, won't he?

01:19:58.200 --> 01:19:58.580
He might.

01:19:59.050 --> 01:19:59.390
Might?

01:20:00.440 --> 01:20:02.500
You look pretty swinging in the wind.

01:20:04.280 --> 01:20:05.320
How does he know it's safe?

01:20:06.360 --> 01:20:07.320
What is the signal?

01:20:08.970 --> 01:20:10.590
A lantern in the attic window,

01:20:11.730 --> 01:20:12.990
waved up and down for danger.

01:20:14.150 --> 01:20:15.730
Across the window when all is clear.

01:20:18.810 --> 01:20:19.370
Come on, Sergeant.

01:20:38.700 --> 01:20:40.500
That is the wrong signal, Lady Blakeney.

01:20:43.060 --> 01:20:44.380
Who keeps a Percy away?

01:20:44.540 --> 01:20:52.700
This is the right one.

01:20:53.370 --> 01:20:54.450
This will bring him here.

01:20:55.920 --> 01:20:58.660
And I can see you are longing to see him, as I am myself.

01:21:01.660 --> 01:21:03.620
What a great actor Sir Percy is.

01:21:04.200 --> 01:21:08.140
A thousand ways to cheat the poor, stupid officials of the Republic.

01:21:09.000 --> 01:21:11.370
Look, costumes, wigs, paint.

01:21:12.800 --> 01:21:13.760
What will he be next?

01:21:14.730 --> 01:21:17.570
In what disguise will he arrive when the clock strikes ten?

01:21:18.720 --> 01:21:21.000
I must arrange a reassuring atmosphere for him.

01:21:23.400 --> 01:21:23.940
An old woman?

01:21:24.850 --> 01:21:25.650
He's overdone that.

01:21:28.040 --> 01:21:28.280
Please.

01:21:30.410 --> 01:21:34.760
What could be more harmful and so useful when it comes to the last offices?

01:21:36.190 --> 01:21:42.940
Sergeant, you shall have the privilege of watching over the Republic's most charming prisoner for the rest of the evening.

01:21:50.560 --> 01:21:54.500
Citizen, the Dragoons should be here at any moment.

01:21:54.680 --> 01:21:56.680
Arrange for a firing squad as soon as they arrive.

01:21:56.960 --> 01:21:58.980
Are you so certain you'll get him?

01:21:59.120 --> 01:21:59.460
Quiet.

01:22:00.640 --> 01:22:02.840
Thanks to a charming friend, I found him there.

01:22:12.040 --> 01:22:12.940
Quarter to ten.

01:22:13.180 --> 01:22:14.720
His way is clear.

01:22:15.160 --> 01:22:16.560
He must not sustain his in the trap.

01:23:09.200 --> 01:23:11.000
How nice of you to wait up for me.

01:23:14.010 --> 01:23:16.130
I had no idea you were in holy order.

01:23:17.190 --> 01:23:20.350
This is only an innocent masquerade, like so many of your own, Sir Percy.

01:23:20.640 --> 01:23:22.100
Ah, but mine was successful.

01:23:22.590 --> 01:23:24.190
Mine might prove successful, yes.

01:23:25.300 --> 01:23:28.570
You walked in here quite freely, but you won't walk out a free man.

01:23:30.030 --> 01:23:31.470
Stop it now, Monsieur Chauvelin.

01:23:31.570 --> 01:23:33.570
The time for laughing is past, Sir Percy.

01:23:34.570 --> 01:23:35.670
I sought you for a year.

01:23:36.380 --> 01:23:38.740
Your energy, your ingenuity, your audacity

01:23:38.740 --> 01:23:39.840
have been quite admirable.

01:23:40.840 --> 01:23:42.950
But now, the game is up.

01:23:43.800 --> 01:23:45.800
Because all the trumps are in your hand, eh?

01:23:46.430 --> 01:23:49.610
Precisely. This house is surrounded by my soldiers.

01:23:50.000 --> 01:23:51.300
And I have only to raise my voice.

01:23:51.340 --> 01:23:53.160
Yes, yes, I see your point.

01:23:53.860 --> 01:23:56.800
I see your point, but suppose,

01:23:57.720 --> 01:23:59.100
suppose I could reach a door.

01:24:00.920 --> 01:24:03.690
The night is black, the sea is mine.

01:24:04.540 --> 01:24:05.160
I make a dash!

01:24:06.730 --> 01:24:08.310
I don't make a dash.

01:24:10.170 --> 01:24:14.360
I don't need to, because one of my friends might shoot you.

01:24:15.560 --> 01:24:16.780
From behind, hidden in that clock.

01:24:19.920 --> 01:24:22.540
Oh, come now. No one really hides in a clock.

01:24:23.570 --> 01:24:29.980
Besides, I still have one more avenue of the sky.

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:32.020
Okay, open to me.

01:24:33.100 --> 01:24:33.560
Don't move!

01:24:35.150 --> 01:24:35.550
Gunpowder!

01:24:35.830 --> 01:24:38.610
If I drop this in here, I fly straight to heaven.

01:24:39.270 --> 01:24:40.330
And you know where you fly to.

01:24:51.140 --> 01:24:52.720
Don't be alarmed, Monsieur Schoenner.

01:24:53.640 --> 01:24:54.740
It's not gunpowder.

01:25:01.180 --> 01:25:03.540
Thank you, Wilmot. We've just arrived in time.

01:25:04.830 --> 01:25:07.010
I've had five delightful minutes with Monsieur Chauvelin.

01:25:07.700 --> 01:25:10.380
I trust it was time enough to get Armand and de Tournai into safety.

01:25:10.620 --> 01:25:11.600
Yes, Percy, they're safe.

01:25:12.240 --> 01:25:14.730
Good. Now we need five minutes.

01:25:15.500 --> 01:25:17.660
Then I shan't trouble you anymore, for the moment.

01:25:18.220 --> 01:25:19.400
We must have the password, Percy.

01:25:20.000 --> 01:25:22.660
The password? Do we have to use force?

01:25:24.780 --> 01:25:25.700
Not at all, Sir Percy.

01:25:26.510 --> 01:25:28.410
The password is the channel is free.

01:25:28.860 --> 01:25:29.260
Splendid.

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:34.320
Wilmot, you get them onto the ship. I'll take care of our friend here and join you in a minute.

01:25:38.720 --> 01:25:41.410
That was quite sensible of you, Monsieur Chauvelin.

01:25:41.660 --> 01:25:46.370
Not at all, Sir Percy. You may go, because I know you'll come back of your own free will.

01:25:47.370 --> 01:25:49.510
You overestimate the charm of your society.

01:25:50.110 --> 01:25:52.830
I told you once the time for jesting was over.

01:25:54.400 --> 01:25:56.080
I have all the trumps in my hand.

01:25:56.940 --> 01:25:59.340
In that room upstairs, there is a woman under arrest.

01:26:00.000 --> 01:26:02.700
has forfeited her life by aiding the enemies of the Republic.

01:26:04.880 --> 01:26:05.320
What woman?

01:26:05.770 --> 01:26:06.810
Lady Blakeney.

01:26:13.140 --> 01:26:14.440
Is the game up, Sir Percy?

01:26:15.520 --> 01:26:17.060
Is this the last adventure?

01:26:17.260 --> 01:26:22.630
I give up, Chauvelin.

01:26:26.390 --> 01:26:26.770
What next?

01:26:27.880 --> 01:26:29.400
There is a firing squad outside.

01:26:32.170 --> 01:26:34.960
And my wife? The Revolutionary Tribunal.

01:26:35.850 --> 01:26:39.650
That means death. It would have meant my death if I had not caught you.

01:26:43.520 --> 01:26:47.510
Don't be alarmed, Sir Percy. I don't want your wife's life.

01:26:48.250 --> 01:26:49.850
She's free the moment you die.

01:26:52.470 --> 01:26:59.200
Enough you a pact. You'll promise to say nothing to her.

01:27:00.480 --> 01:27:05.360
If you send her on to my ship immediately, I'll walk up in front of your firing squad.

01:27:10.900 --> 01:27:11.380
I accept.

01:27:13.210 --> 01:27:16.790
Sergeant, bring the lady down.

01:27:30.000 --> 01:27:32.420
I wanted to give my life to save you. Forgive me, Percy.

01:27:32.500 --> 01:27:34.830
My dear, it's nothing. I'm in no danger.

01:27:35.030 --> 01:27:46.940
I want to die with you.

01:27:49.700 --> 01:27:50.460
Don't move, Chevrolet.

01:27:52.330 --> 01:27:53.890
Parting would be too cruel, even for you.

01:27:55.480 --> 01:27:57.040
Just take her out while she's still unconscious.

01:27:58.070 --> 01:27:59.390
My boat should be at the point by now.

01:28:01.470 --> 01:28:07.970
Goodbye, my sweet. It's good to know that you love me a little.

01:28:25.440 --> 01:28:27.520
Send this lady to the English ship around the point.

01:28:27.990 --> 01:28:29.730
If anybody attempts to land, shoot!

01:28:30.640 --> 01:28:32.850
Yes, sir. You two go with him.

01:28:33.090 --> 01:28:46.910
Like poetry, Mr. Chauvelin.

01:28:47.640 --> 01:28:49.500
That damned, elusive Pimpernel.

01:28:49.740 --> 01:28:52.850
No, no, I mean, uh, poetry.

01:28:56.400 --> 01:28:57.840
This other Eden, demi-paradise.

01:29:00.000 --> 01:29:04.120
Fortress built by nature for herself against infection and the hand of war.

01:29:07.100 --> 01:29:08.600
This happy breed of men.

01:29:09.200 --> 01:29:10.180
This little world.

01:29:12.250 --> 01:29:15.370
This precious stone set in the silver sea.

01:29:17.460 --> 01:29:18.680
This blessed plot.

01:29:19.680 --> 01:29:20.140
This earth.

01:29:21.040 --> 01:29:21.680
This realm.

01:29:24.180 --> 01:29:24.580
England.

01:29:28.040 --> 01:29:29.140
Oh, damn me, I forget the rest.

01:29:38.050 --> 01:29:49.450
Now it appears I shan't have time to remember.

01:30:51.110 --> 01:30:52.530
I have to come back to my hat.

01:30:53.120 --> 01:30:54.700
It's such a cursed good hat, you know.

01:30:59.240 --> 01:30:59.980
Don't look at me like that.

01:31:00.000 --> 01:31:03.390
That! Sink me if you don't think I'm my own ghost.

01:31:04.260 --> 01:31:04.600
Durock!

01:31:05.310 --> 01:31:06.210
Captain Durock?

01:31:07.300 --> 01:31:11.380
I'm afraid it'll be an hour or so before poor Captain Durock will be able to resume his duty.

01:31:11.740 --> 01:31:16.620
I regret that I struck him rather violently, Father.

01:31:17.120 --> 01:31:17.580
Cheat him!

01:31:18.450 --> 01:31:21.110
Always so impulsive, my dear Mr. Shogner.

01:31:23.890 --> 01:31:26.790
This, er, is my firing squad.

01:31:27.280 --> 01:31:29.960
Allow me to present Foukes, Dewhurst, Hastings.

01:31:30.120 --> 01:31:36.400
belleville and the rest but of course you know all about them you look rather excited

01:31:36.400 --> 01:31:55.230
children i think you need cooling down so just a peaceful little nap like we had in the grenville

01:32:20.090 --> 01:32:22.090
It's you, darling.

01:32:23.760 --> 01:32:25.700
Chevalin said you'd be free the moment I die.

01:32:29.080 --> 01:32:29.860
Won't be a moment.

01:32:33.320 --> 01:32:39.050
Look, Marguerite, England.
